  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0154, and it contains three tables: user, product, and supply_and_demand_relationship. The user table has the following columns: username, password, gender, phone_number, id_number, email, and user_id. The user_id column is the primary key. The product table has the following columns: title, category, price, images, content, validity_period, contact_person, phone_number, and product_id. The product_id column is the primary key. The supply_and_demand_relationship table has the following columns: user_id, product_id, supply_and_demand_id, and supply_and_demand_type. The supply_and_demand_id column is the primary key. The user_id and product_id columns are foreign keys that reference the user and product tables, respectively. The ON DELETE CASCADE and ON UPDATE CASCADE clauses specify that if a user or product is deleted or updated, the corresponding supply_and_demand_relationship records should also be deleted or updated.",
  "gold_question": "A commodity supply and demand system is designed to facilitate user registration and login, personal information management, product posting and management, search and browsing, as well as the display of supply and demand information matching. The functional requirements are as follows:\n\nThe user table management stores relevant user information, including user ID, as well as username, password, gender, phone number, ID number, and email, which are used for user registration, login, and personal information management.\n\nThe product table management stores various types of product information, including title, category, price, images, content, validity period, contact person, and phone number, supporting the functions of product posting and management.\n\nThe supply and demand relationship table management uses the supply and demand ID as an identifier, combines user ID and product ID, and specifies the type of supply and demand to record the relationship between users and products, thereby achieving the function of matching and displaying supply and demand information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0154.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0154\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `id_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `images` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `validity_period` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supply_and_demand_relationship` (\n  `supply_and_demand_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supply_and_demand_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supply_and_demand_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `supply_and_demand_relationship_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `supply_and_demand_relationship_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
